                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "This game is insanely good, Slay the Spire levels good. I played it a bunch on mobile and decided to buy it on PC to support the devs. The equipment combinations are crazy interesting and fun, the enemies super varied and quite insane at times, the classes all play differently, etc. It has an enormous amount of content and replayability too.\n\nThe game plays like your classic card roguelite but with more enemies and kinda crazier and more punishing mechanics. Similarly, your deck of cards has some insanely strong cards, even when compared to other games in the genre. The game lets you change your starting decks of cards which won't change during the run, so it's not a matter of getting that one God run, but rather how good you are at using the deck you picked. In that sense the game plays a ton like magic or hearthstone in the best way possible.\n\nThe visuals are a subjective matter, I personally love the gritty pixel art, but it wouldn't surprise me that people get turned off by it.\n\nThere are a few issues, notably the game needs to be more clear with secret unlocks. The subclasses should also unlock differently than basically \"play the subclass to unlock the actual subclass\", or balancing the subclasses unlocked to go more in depth than just adding minor stat changes. The level ups many times feel quite useless too, and some are tied to actual RNG which is not great, same with that one archer card, although in his case it makes sense thematically.\n\nIf you want a more puzzle based Slay the Spire/etc definitely pick this up, it's definitely up there. Pretty sad the remake was cancelled too, because balance wise this game only need a few little tweaks to be basically perfect.",
